% =============================================================================
% trill sequent rules — the ○ next-time modality over the graded-fixpoint surface
% =============================================================================
%
% trill's backward judgment = [gill.rules, grill.rules] (inherited BY REFERENCE —
% calculus.load takes a rules-file list; gill's whole graded fragment plus the four
% μ/ν unfold rules) plus the single ○ tick rule below. The list
% [gill.rules, grill.rules, trill.rules] is assembled in trill's loader.
%
% The ○ rule is VERBATIM rill's: the whole-context TICK. It is grade-agnostic —
% the generic @tick machinery (focused.js bypass + kernel.js re-derivation) reads
% the ○ connective from the descriptor and strips one ○ from every consumable
% formula, whatever grade those resources carry. Grades ride the tick unchanged,
% exactly as they ride the μ/ν body under grill's unfold rules.
% =============================================================================

@formulas A, B, C

% Whole-context TICK (○R + ○-elimination, THY_0043 §temporal-cut): advance the
% whole sequent one step — G ; ○Δ |- ○C <- G ; Δ |- C. Fires only when the
% succedent is ○C AND every linear formula is ○-wrapped; strips one ○ from each,
% persistent G passes through. Empty-Δ case = promotion-shaped ○R (introduction);
% non-empty case = ○-elimination / temporal cut (applicative ○(A⊸B),○A ⊢ ○B).
% NON-COLLAPSING: ○a ⊬ a (succedent not ○), a ⊬ ○a (context not ○-wrapped).
next_r: G ; |- O A
  <- G ; |- A
  @pretty "○"
  @invertible false
  @tick true.
